# tests/atomic_groups/atomic_ceiling.rxt -- module `atomic-groups` ([M6.4.2]):
# THE R3a FAMILY -- patterns whose CUT match ends LATER than their UNCUT twin's.
#
# WHY A WHOLE FILE FOR ONE SHAPE. The default engine is a hybrid: a
# capture-erased forward+reverse DFA pair runs as a prefilter and hands the VM a
# window. That DFA necessarily answers for the UNCUT language -- subset
# construction keeps every alternative alive, which is exactly the NON-atomic
# semantics -- so its span END is NOT an upper bound on the cut match's end:
#
#     (?>a|ab)c|abcd   on "abcd"   is (0,4)
#     (?:a|ab)c|abcd   on "abcd"   is (0,3)      <- the uncut twin
#
# Measured at 122 refuting cells over 17,640, and -- on the EMITTED prefilter
# rather than inferred from an oracle -- 114 cells across 42 patterns carrying a
# "prefilter-window" ceiling AND a window end strictly below the cut match's
# end. Without RULE H3 (src/gen/emit_vm.c: the MRL ceiling is switched off on a
# cut-bearing artifact) those are silent match losses in the DEFAULT engine, on
# patterns the VM engine gets right. The cells here are the behavioural half;
# the structural half is tests/codegen/'s `[M6.4-ATOMIC rule 1]`, and the two
# arms of tests/atomic_groups/run_atomic_diff.sh are what compare the engines.
#
# BOTH CLAMP POPULATIONS ARE PRESENT, which is R31 C5's requirement rather than
# thoroughness: `RX_VM_PRUNE_CEILING` is THREE-valued, and with `nclamp == 0` an
# artifact stamps "none", declares no `window_end` local and has no ceiling to
# get wrong. Over the design's own 46 R3a patterns the histogram is
# {prefilter-window 42, none 4}, so a file made only of the first cannot see a
# ceiling bug on the second -- and the codegen rule is RED on the second if it
# is not scoped. Section 2 is the `nclamp == 0` population.
#
# EVERY EXPECTATION IN THIS FILE WAS PRODUCED BY libpcre2 10.46, not written by
# hand: a generator drove every (pattern, subject, startpos) cell through the
# ctypes binding at docs/design/eng_brep_measurements/probes/pcre2_ctypes.py and
# emitted the answer. python3 `re` was driven over the SAME cells in the same
# pass, and a block carries `# pcre2-only` exactly where python disagreed or
# could not compile the pattern -- detected, never assumed. 13 of 729 cells
# diverge across this directory, and they are the four families Appendix B.3 of
# the design names: `\K`/`\G` (python cannot express them at all), the BRACE
# possessive over a two-exit body (python cuts PER ITERATION, PCRE2 at the GROUP
# EXIT), U9 (libpcre2's own recorded oddity), and scoped `(?i)` inside a group
# (python rejects the pattern).
#
# `ms`/`ns` CELLS SWEEP EVERY STARTPOS IN [0, n], not a chosen few. The cut
# makes "the leftmost candidate is not the leftmost match" an ORDINARY
# occurrence rather than an edge case -- `(?>a|ab)c` on "abc" is NO MATCH while
# its uncut twin matches (0,3) -- so which start the search reaches, and what it
# answers there, is the axis this construct moves.

# ====================================================================
# THE R3a FAMILY: the cut match ends LATER than the uncut twin's
# ====================================================================

pattern (?>a|ab)c|abcd
features atomic-groups
m "abcd" 0 4
ns 1 "abcd"
ns 2 "abcd"
ns 3 "abcd"
ns 4 "abcd"

pattern (?>ab|a)b|abcd
features atomic-groups
m "abcd" 0 4
ns 1 "abcd"
ns 2 "abcd"
ns 3 "abcd"
ns 4 "abcd"

pattern x*(?>a|ab)c|abcd
features atomic-groups
m "abcd" 0 4
ns 1 "abcd"
ns 2 "abcd"
ns 3 "abcd"
ns 4 "abcd"
m "xabcd" 1 5
ms 1 "xabcd" 1 5
ns 2 "xabcd"
ns 3 "xabcd"
ns 4 "xabcd"
ns 5 "xabcd"

pattern a*(?>b|bc)d|abcde
features atomic-groups
m "abcde" 0 5
ns 1 "abcde"
ns 2 "abcde"
ns 3 "abcde"
ns 4 "abcde"
ns 5 "abcde"
n "bcde"
ns 1 "bcde"
ns 2 "bcde"
ns 3 "bcde"
ns 4 "bcde"

pattern (?>a|ab)c+|abcd
features atomic-groups
m "abcd" 0 4
ns 1 "abcd"
ns 2 "abcd"
ns 3 "abcd"
ns 4 "abcd"
n "abccd"
ns 1 "abccd"
ns 2 "abccd"
ns 3 "abccd"
ns 4 "abccd"
ns 5 "abccd"

# ====================================================================
# THE `nclamp == 0` POPULATION -- artifacts that stamp "none"
# ====================================================================

pattern (?>a|ab)[cd]{1,2}|abcd
features atomic-groups
m "abcd" 0 4
ns 1 "abcd"
ns 2 "abcd"
ns 3 "abcd"
ns 4 "abcd"

pattern (?>ab|a)b|abcd
features atomic-groups
m "abcd" 0 4
ns 1 "abcd"
ns 2 "abcd"
ns 3 "abcd"
ns 4 "abcd"
